    "round_robin": "Within each input, group source records by exact ordered final reactant tuple in first-occurrence route order. One selected-rule entry per still-active tuple each round. Keep each source graph as a separate upstream context.",
    "rule_order": "Use each input current v14 outer_rules_selected exact order/list, including listed fallback flags; never reorder by source product or saved model output. Exclude only that tuple\u2019s original final rule. No role permutation. A repeated rule ID entry remains a charged visit but cannot be selected as a second distinct alternative for the same tuple.",
    "eligibility": "Charge one inspection for every visited rule-list entry, including original/unsupported/invalid entries. Require same reactant count, complete strict template_maps with no issues, and exact per-slot HasSubstructMatch(useChirality=True). Stop this tuple after its first two role-compatible strict-template alternatives, including zero-product or gate-failed calls; do not walk further based on products. role_checks counts explicit preselection checks. Rules.apply repeats at most three role checks per generation call; its bounded calls and a conservative internal-check upper bound are reported separately.",
    "generation": "Rules.apply(rule_id, ordered_original_final_reactants, product_limit16) once per selected tuple/rule. Attach each returned product to every unchanged upstream graph variant of that tuple by changing only final rule_id and final product. Preserve all raw truncation flags, gate failures and audit-unassessed graphs. No graph deduplication is implicit: retain every source lineage and explicitly count any identical candidate graphs if they occur.",
    "pregates": "Use unchanged v14 HitStereoAnchors, hop changed-scaffold/required core, _check_stereo, selective preflight/POLAR, property thresholds, and original-hit 2048-bit Morgan Tanimoto, in that order. Same fixed per-input effective config.",
    "audit": "Audit gate-passing new graphs with audit_route product_limit64, strict_eligible only; cap64 new audits/input. Original16 graph controls each get same pregates plus fresh verify_route64 and audit_route64. Control costs separate from new-audit cap. The fixed original control audits are separate diagnostic work from the at-most64 new audits, with combined per-input maximum69. This does not assert a future production total64 audit budget can be met; future production must share its original total across old/new candidates.",
    "analyzer": "Candidate set and all work counters must be terminal and SHA-frozen first. Then compare only exact unchanged reactant/reagent request and pinned provenance to previously saved actual-v2 raw beams; no new predictor/model calls. A tokenizer-only read is allowed for input token/beam validation if reviewed; model weights never loaded. The offline borrowed methods in evidence.py/forward_support.py/common.py, plus tokenizer/RDKit/Python runtime and analysis-freeze bytes, are checked before tokenization and after analysis.",
